Modified files
--------------

Each file listed below is a modified file: the derived material was translated
into Spanish and adapted to the editorial method of this collection, and the
text around it is original to the collection. The upstream file names in each
entry identify where the derived passages come from.

### `skills/maquetacion-editorial/references/antipatrones.md`

Derived from `impeccable` and from `better-typography`. Modified: translated
into Spanish and rewritten.

From `impeccable` (`reference/craft-floor.md`, `reference/new-work.md`,
`reference/typeset.md`, `reference/layout.md`) the file keeps, in translated
and adapted form, the catalogue of design tics and part of the review
vocabulary: the cluster of a warm cream ground with a high-contrast serif and
a terracotta accent; same-size cards as the page structure; the kicker above a
heading; section numbers 01 / 02 / 03; hard offset shadows; monospace as a
costume for "technical"; Unicode glyphs and emoji standing in for an icon
system; the split between reading and operating surfaces and persuasion and
experience surfaces; and the squint test.

From `better-typography` (`SKILL.md`,
`wrapping-and-punctuation.md`) the file keeps the five-column incident report,
a three-level severity scale and the rule that a blocking verdict stands
while a high-severity finding remains. It also adapts the character-based
line-measure checks and the guidance on typographic punctuation, including
non-breaking spaces.

### `skills/maquetacion-editorial/references/tipografia.md`

Derived from `better-typography` (`SKILL.md`,
`wrapping-and-punctuation.md`). Modified: translated into Spanish and adapted.
The file keeps the sentence that screen designs rarely use more than three
fonts, and adapts the character-based line-measure guidance, typographic marks
instead of keyboard substitutes, and the single-character ellipsis.

### `skills/maquetacion-editorial/references/programa.md`

Derived from `canvas-design` (`SKILL.md`). Modified: translated into Spanish
and adapted. The file keeps the requirement that nothing overlaps and nothing
falls outside the margins, with breathing room between elements; the warning
against disguising weaknesses by adding frames, grounds or ornament at the end
instead of refining what exists; and the idea of writing a short statement of
concept before composing.

### `skills/maquetacion-editorial/SKILL.md`

Derived from `better-typography` (`SKILL.md`). Modified: translated into
Spanish and adapted. The five columns of the incident report in step 8,
`Gravedad | Dónde | Antes | Después | Por qué`, are a translation of the
reporting table of that skill.

